# ── Read this before adding anything ─────────────────────────────────────────
#
# `.env` is NOT ignored here, and that is deliberate.
#
# Every host directory ships a committed `.env` holding published demo values,
# because constraint #6 is that `docker compose up` works on a fresh clone with
# no flags and no setup step. Ignoring `.env` is the reflex, and it would
# silently break the quickstart for everyone who clones this repo.
#
# Nothing in this repository is a secret. The demo images ship their own
# credentials by design. If you ever find yourself wanting to add a real secret
# here, that is the signal that it does not belong in this repo at all.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Local overrides — these DO get ignored, so a user can override the committed
# defaults without git showing them as modified.
.env.local
*.env.local

# The golden SQL artifact is injected at build time by CI and is far too large
# (and too data-bearing) to live in git.
**/demo.sql
**/demo.sql.gz

# OS / editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# Local rehearsal wheels are a build input, never a repo artifact.
#
# Listed per host rather than as `**/wheels/*.whl` because that is how it was
# started — but note that the per-host form means ADDING A HOST SILENTLY OPTS
# IT OUT. The netbox wheel was staged for commit before anyone noticed. If a
# fourth host appears, add its line here at the same time as its directory.
nautobot/wheels/*.whl
paperless/wheels/*.whl
netbox/wheels/*.whl

# The Paperless demo estate has TWO halves. `**/demo.sql.gz` above covers the
# database; this covers the media tree the database points at. Both are build
# artifacts produced by paperless/seed/seed.sh, and the media tarball is a
# multi-megabyte binary that has no business in git.
**/media.tar.gz

# The generated document corpus. Reproducible from paperless/seed/corpus.py,
# so committing it would add binary churn for no gain.
paperless/seed/out/
